**Theorem 9.1 (all three original upper budgets and actual BOTH-bit attainment).** If a preparer succeeds at $N,P,L$ under Definition 3.3, the literal-only normalization in Theorem 8.3 succeeds at those same upper budgets with the same installed preparer graph and the immutable $T,e_0,e_1$. Both original bits remain actually attained. No pointwise equality $\sigma'(u)=\sigma(u)$ is asserted.

Proof. Fix any actual new $u'$. The inclusion $\mathcal J_{A'}\subseteq\mathcal J_A$ supplies one actual old $u$ with the identical two full reply vectors and whole target. The preparations begin at the same common state. At an equal Read state the respective actual replies agree, so the unchanged successor functions give the same next state. Induction therefore gives the same state path, same paid call count and same original Halt bit $z$. Old success supplies a Halt within $P$ calls.

The actual handoff enters the same literal state $e_z$ of the unchanged serving table. Its full reply vector also agrees on this same pair $u',u$, so serving-state induction gives the identical selected-entry path, call count, terminal Halt and fixed complete output. That output is $F(u)=F(u')$, reached within $L$ calls. A wrong or nonterminating unselected entry imposes no condition. Preparation and serving have been compared on one common old source, not on separately chosen realizations.

Conversely, choose an old actual origin attaining bit $z$, for either $z=0$ or $z=1$. The reverse relation inclusion gives a new actual origin with the same whole triple. Its common-start path reaches the same original bit Halt. Thus both bits persist. Their witnesses are different because one fixed source has one deterministic preparation output. Installed state counts are exactly unchanged, so the original $N$ remains valid. Each repeated, empty, absent or leaf-continuation query still corresponds to a real Read visit. Initial Halts and Halts just after a last allowed call require no extra call. State sharing and different-source union cycles require no copies or clocks. $\square$

The comparison also weakly decreases the preparation's literal sum along its matched path, since each state's word individually weakly shortens. This compares new $u'$ with its joint old witness $u$, rather than comparing the two preparations on the identical origin. The declared synthesis problem uses the original $N,P,L$, without treating this observation as a physical resource bound.

